# Portal geography: operational release procedure

Development branch: `feat/portal-geography-pipeline`. Functional commits: `2c8f6da`, `12d113f`.
This closure adds operational tests and release documentation only. No new runtime
architecture, dependency, migration, AVM or production change.

## Validation boundary

ARM64 is emulated with Docker Desktop/QEMU on Windows amd64, not native Oracle.
The local representative base uses Python 3.13.14, Debian 13.6 and the same 81
distribution versions inventoried READ ONLY from Oracle. Already archived local
ingestion v3 and deployed thumbnail sources reconstruct the relevant code in the
older local validation base. Source comparisons normalize CRLF/LF only.
The production image itself was not exported. This is not a byte-identical copy
of all production layers, nor an Oracle performance/load certification.

The actual release Dockerfile still overlays only ten runtime files onto the
verified current production image. The representative base/reconstruction is
strictly local validation material and must **not** replace that production base.

PostgreSQL validation uses official 16.14-alpine on an internal Docker network,
synthetic listings and archived HTML only. The application/test client is ARM64;
the PostgreSQL server is native amd64, same PostgreSQL release as Oracle's ARM64
server. No Oracle DB dump or production credentials enter these tests.
Tests refuse other database names/hosts/users and create/drop only their random
`portal_geo_op_*` schemas. Real simultaneous sessions, row locks, SKIP LOCKED,
commits, cancellations and rollback execute against PostgreSQL. The per-worker
request budget is independent: two invocations with budget1 may make two distinct
requests total, never two requests for the same reserved publication.

The harness permits 30-second statements for QEMU client round trips, retaining
a strict 1.5-second lock timeout and PostgreSQL lock-wait logging at 100ms.
These are test settings, not production configuration or a latency target.
Initial incorrect fixture parsing and short QEMU timeouts are retained in local
validation logs; they are not represented as passing tests.

## Promotion and preflight (not executed)

1. Promote only the geography commits plus this operational closure, preserving
   the deployed History v3 prerequisite. Do not replace the dirty local UI branch
   or all Oracle checkout files. Review `git diff 5adc256..HEAD` and the ten runtime
   paths in `Dockerfile.portal-geography-overlay`.
2. Re-read current image/tag, effective settings, mounts, schema0021, API health,
   three Compose file paths and Portal/Yapo timer state. Abort/reconcile if any
   relevant deployed source hash has changed from the recorded baseline.
3. Preserve existing private configuration through the previously approved secure
   backup mechanism. Verify a current PostgreSQL dump/globals and retain the
   existing image by immutable release tag. No migration is required or permitted
   by this release; do not rerun History0021 on production.
4. Build the production overlay on the verified current image, not the older
   Oracle checkout or local representative base:

   ```sh
   docker image inspect valoria-thumbnails:shared-v2-20261008 --format '{{.Id}}'
   # Must still equal sha256:85b7c668299eb7883ef668f422583adc226d5d1e21fbc1d08ae13de82bf88147
   docker image tag sha256:85b7c668299eb7883ef668f422583adc226d5d1e21fbc1d08ae13de82bf88147 valoria-portal-geo-rollback:20261011
   docker build --pull=false --network=none --platform=linux/arm64 \
     -f Dockerfile.portal-geography-overlay \
     --build-arg BASE_IMAGE=valoria-thumbnails:shared-v2-20261008 \
     -t valoria-portal-geo:<approved-commit> .
   ```

   This is a future authorized release operation. Validate the resulting image
   digest and record it before changing the API service. Retain the previous tag.

## Stage A â€” code deployment, Portal paused (not executed)

The READ ONLY inventory found exactly these existing Compose files:

- `docker-compose.oracle.yml`
- `deploy/ingestion-v3-20261004.override.yml`
- `deploy/thumbnails-v2-20261008.override.yml`

The new code-only override sets Portal false and geo budget0 explicitly, leaving
all existing History, volumes, Yapo and scheduler configuration inherited.

After deployment approval and preflight, from `/home/ubuntu/apps/valoria`:

```sh
export PORTAL_GEO_RELEASE_IMAGE='valoria-portal-geo:<approved-commit>'
docker compose -p valoria_oracle_beta \
  -f docker-compose.oracle.yml \
  -f deploy/ingestion-v3-20261004.override.yml \
  -f deploy/thumbnails-v2-20261008.override.yml \
  -f deploy/portal-geography-code.override.yml \
  up -d --no-deps --no-build api
```

No timer command, manual scrape, migration or history/data rewrite belongs here.
Before calling deployment successful:

1. Check expected image ID, API running/healthy and zero restart loop.
2. Require HTTP200/`status=ok` from `/health` and `/api/v1/health`. Check DB SELECT1
   and Redis PING against existing service dependencies; inspect no private config.
3. Read only the named flags: `portal_http_enabled=false`, geo budget0, attempts3,
   cooldown24, History ON; preserve scheduler/workers effective baseline.
4. Verify authenticated read-only Radar/watchlist/thumbnail responses and existing
   Tasar contract/routes. Observe normal user flows; no synthetic production
   valuation writes or scrape is necessary for code-only acceptance.
5. Require Portal timer still inactive, Yapo timer unchanged, no new Portal source
   requests/observations caused by release, schema still0021, no import/DB errors.
   Roll back on any attributable health, authentication or existing-flow regression.

## Exact Stage A rollback (prepared, not executed)

Keep Portal inactive and reuse the **same four Compose files**. Set the immutable
retained image tag; recreate only API:

```sh
export PORTAL_GEO_RELEASE_IMAGE='valoria-portal-geo-rollback:20261011'
docker compose -p valoria_oracle_beta \
  -f docker-compose.oracle.yml \
  -f deploy/ingestion-v3-20261004.override.yml \
  -f deploy/thumbnails-v2-20261008.override.yml \
  -f deploy/portal-geography-code.override.yml \
  up -d --no-deps --no-build api
```

Recheck the expected old image ID and Stage A health/flags checks. The old Settings
ignores the additive geo variables. No DB downgrade, restore, observation deletion
or inverse backfill: retain any lat/lon/provenance already written and History ON.
Preserve the thumbnail volume and Yapo timer. A database restoration is not part
of a code rollback.

## Stage B â€” separately authorized activation (not executed)

Code deployment is **not** permission to reactivate Portal. A later authorization
must specify Portal acquisition resumption and its existing timer/service controls,
as well as geo budget1, max attempts3 and cooldown24h. The Stage A false/zero
override must be superseded explicitly in that later approved configuration;
do not merely change a lower-precedence environment file.

Observe the next normal cycle and subsequent cooldown/reobservation cycle. Record
commercial versus extra/reused requests, accepted/missing/rejected/blocked and
exhausted counts, canonical coverage, MLC/provenance agreement, history events,
wall time, locks, errors, storage and resources. A pin with unknown physical
accuracy stays unknown. Budget1 permits at most one additional detail per normal
invocation, not one per card, and no new job/timer.

Stop enrichment on accepted identity/context conflicts, unexpected overwrites,
privacy incidents, request-budget violations, persistent blocks, transaction/lock
errors or storage pressure. First return the extra budget to0 through the approved
operational configuration; keep/pause Portal if acquisition itself is unhealthy.
Do not retry through challenges, bypass403/429 or erase evidence. Stage B rollback
also restores the Stage A Portal false/zero configuration before code rollback.

## Evidence

Machine-readable final evidence: `portal-geography-operational-validation.json`.
PostgreSQL test: `tests/integration_pg/test_portal_geography_operational.py`.
The previously excluded Yapo test is rerun against both baseline and candidate;
the unchanged CLP-price-zero rejection is inherited, not repaired by this release.
The broader inherited suite is not claimed globally green.


## Repeating the isolated PostgreSQL tests

With the validated local ARM64 image present, from this repository:

```sh
docker compose -f tests/integration_pg/compose.portal-geography.yml up --abort-on-container-exit --exit-code-from validation
docker compose -f tests/integration_pg/compose.portal-geography.yml down
```

The Compose file is a repeatability recipe for the same image/test/network/DB
configuration exercised during closure; its local roles/JWT are synthetic test
values. No persistent data or host port is mounted. Without the explicit opt-in
URL the test class is skipped by ordinary pytest. Production paths and credentials
are never accepted by this harness.
